L0S shell, on an L0 microkernel. Type help for the commands.
l0s> l0s> 1280x800
l0s> draw: no command blah
[pid 9 exited with 1]
l0s> draw: no color nocolor
[pid 10 exited with 1]
l0s> usage: draw COMMAND, one of
  line X0 Y0 X1 Y1 [COLOR]   a line, both ends included
  circle CX CY R [COLOR]     a circle's outline
  disc CX CY R [COLOR]       a filled circle
  rect X Y W H [COLOR]       a rectangle's outline
  fill X Y W H [COLOR]       a filled rectangle
  clear [COLOR]              the whole desktop, black unless given
  char X Y CODE [COLOR]      a character, 8 by 16, its code 32 to 126
  round X Y W H R [COLOR]    a filled rectangle, its corners of radius R
  button X Y KIND LABEL      a button: regular, flat, suggested, destructive
  splash [PERCENT]           the wallpaper, as bright as given
  restore X Y W H            the wallpaper back, as splash last drew it
  size                       print the desktop's width and height
  font                       print a character's width and height
Pixels count from 0, 0 at the top left. COLOR is white unless given:
white black red green blue yellow cyan magenta amber gray, RRGGBB, or
Adwaita's: blue_1 to blue_5, and green_, yellow_, orange_, red_, purple_,
brown_, light_, and dark_ the same; accent destructive success warning error.
Commands separated by ; are done together, and shown at once.
l0s> 